description:
A mapped file is just a span of bytes (lesson 3.04). Navigate one without copying it. The file holds records, each a 4-byte little-endian length followed by that many bytes:

```cpp
struct Index { std::vector<std::size_t> offsets; bool truncated; };

Index buildIndex(std::span<const std::uint8_t> file);
std::span<const std::uint8_t> recordAt(std::span<const std::uint8_t> file, const Index& index, std::size_t i);
std::optional<std::size_t> findRecord(std::span<const std::uint8_t> file, const Index& index, std::string_view text);
```

- **buildIndex** walks the file from the start and records the offset of each record's **data** (just after its length). If a length runs past the end of the file, it stops there and sets `truncated` (a file cut short by a crash, or corrupt). Trailing bytes too short for a length also count as truncated.
- **recordAt** returns a view of record `i`'s data **inside the file** (no copy), or an empty span for an index out of range.
- **findRecord** returns the number of the first record whose bytes equal `text`.

